Package: EDE
Title: Extinction Date Estimation from Sighting Records
Version: 0.3.0
Authors@R: person("Rodrigo Fonseca", "Villa", email = "rodrigo03.villa@gmail.com",
           role = c("aut", "cre"),
           comment = c(ORCID = "0009-0005-2938-2270"))
Maintainer: Rodrigo Fonseca Villa <rodrigo03.villa@gmail.com>
Description: Infers the extinction of a species from a time-ordered record of
    sightings, collecting methods from the sighting-record and
    stratigraphic-range literature under one interface. Includes endpoint
    estimators (Robson & Whitlock, 1964; Strauss & Sadler, 1989; Roberts &
    Solow, 2003), frequentist persistence tests (Solow, 1993a, 1993b; Burgman,
    Grimson & Ferson, 1995; Solow & Roberts, 2003; Solow, 2005; McInerny,
    Roberts, Davy & Cribb, 2006; Jarić & Ebenhard, 2010), Bayesian models
    (Rout, Salomon & McCarthy, 2009; Caley & Barry, 2014), methods for
    sightings of uncertain reliability (Thompson et al., 2013; Jarić &
    Roberts, 2014; Lee et al., 2014; Brook, Buettel & Jarić, 2019; Kodikara
    et al., 2020, 2021), models combining records and
    surveys (Thompson et al., 2017, 2019), and confidence intervals on the
    end-points of fossil ranges (Marshall, 1994, 1997; Weiss & Marshall,
    1999). Every method is tested against the published examples of its
    source paper and returns a common result class; persistence tests are
    inverted to give one-sided upper confidence bounds.
